1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,400
A forger got one letter wrong and still made millions.

2
00:00:04,240 --> 00:00:08,880
Early nineteen eighties, West Germany. Konrad Kujau sells old war souvenirs.

3
00:00:09,460 --> 00:00:13,340
Then he starts hand-writing fake Hitler diaries. Yeah, really.

4
00:00:13,860 --> 00:00:16,220
He sells them under a fake name, through a middleman.

5
00:00:16,640 --> 00:00:20,940
And guess who bought it? A star reporter at Stern, a giant German magazine.

6
00:00:21,520 --> 00:00:23,680
Double-tap if you can already tell how this ends.

7
00:00:24,220 --> 00:00:28,580
That reporter, Gerd Heidemann, got his bosses to pay about nine million marks.

8
00:00:29,040 --> 00:00:32,880
Marks were German money back then, so that's a stupid amount for some notebooks.

9
00:00:33,600 --> 00:00:37,720
Oh, and Heidemann secretly kept a big chunk of it for himself. Classy.

10
00:00:38,160 --> 00:00:42,020
In April nineteen eighty-three, the magazine told the whole damn world.

11
00:00:42,480 --> 00:00:44,640
But nobody bothered to look closely at the cover.

12
00:00:45,120 --> 00:00:48,760
The initials? Plastic letters from a shop, and they said F H.

13
00:00:49,340 --> 00:00:51,260
Send this to the friend who'd still miss it.

14
00:00:51,660 --> 00:00:55,560
Hitler's first name starts with an A. The forger couldn't even get that right.

15
00:00:55,960 --> 00:01:00,740
Then the national archives tested the paper and the ink. Both were modern as hell.

16
00:01:01,280 --> 00:01:04,820
Less than two weeks after the big announcement, they called it a crude forgery.

17
00:01:06,280 --> 00:01:09,040
Translation? A cheap, obvious fake that a quick test could have caught.

18
00:01:09,440 --> 00:01:11,240
Follow, 'cause now the sentence drops.

19
00:01:11,860 --> 00:01:15,680
In nineteen eighty-five, a Hamburg court convicted Kujau and the reporter.

20
00:01:16,160 --> 00:01:18,360
Each of them got about four and a half years in prison.

21
00:01:18,860 --> 00:01:22,140
All those millions, and they never checked two letters on the front.

22
00:01:22,680 --> 00:01:24,620
Would you have spotted it? Yes or no.

